  "result": "JWT `exp` field is Unix seconds. `Date.now()` returns milliseconds.\n\n```js\n// Bug: comparing ms vs seconds \u2014 exp always looks huge, never expired\nif (Date.now() > payload.exp) { ... }\n\n// Fix:\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp) { ... }\n// or\nif (Date.now() > payload.exp * 1000) { ... }\n```\n\nAlso add clock skew buffer to avoid race conditions at exact expiry:\n\n```js\nconst CLOCK_SKEW_SEC = 30;\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp + CLOCK_SKEW_SEC) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\nTwo checks while here: verify `exp` field exists before comparing, and confirm token was signed with your key before trusting any payload field.",
